{
  "name": "burying-beetle",
  "_about": "The sexton or burying beetle (Nicrophorus vespillo), 1.8 cm long: flat and black, the wing cases cut off square so the last three segments of the abdomen show bare behind them; two jagged ORANGE bands across the wing cases; clubbed antennae, the club orange; a round pronotum with golden hair along its front edge; strong legs, the hind tibiae curved. It buries dead mice. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
